import json,statistics as st,html,sys,collections,math
from pathlib import Path
p=Path(sys.argv[1]);rows=[json.loads(s) for s in (p/'games.jsonl').read_text().splitlines()];assert len(rows)==60
mean=lambda a:round(st.mean(a),2) if a else None
q=lambda a,f:sorted(a)[min(len(a)-1,int(f*len(a)))] if a else None
summary=[]
for n in [None,2,3,4]:
 for policy in [None,'self','mixed']:
  a=[r for r in rows if (n is None or r['players']==n) and (policy is None or r['cohort']==policy)];f=[r for r in a if r.get('endReason')=='finish'];prices=[x for r in a for x in r.get('prices',[])];actions=[r['actions'] for r in f]
  summary.append(dict(players=n or 'all',policy=policy or 'all',games=len(a),finished=len(f),stalled=sum(r['status']=='stalled' for r in a),censored=sum(r['status']=='censored' for r in a),failed=sum(r['status']=='failed' for r in a),gap=mean([r['range'] for r in f]),third=mean([r['thirdLag'] for r in f]),actionsMean=mean(actions),actionsMedian=st.median(actions) if actions else None,actionsP90=q(actions,.9),auctionMean=mean(prices),auctionMedian=st.median(prices) if prices else None,auctionP90=q(prices,.9)))
finish=[r for r in rows if r.get('endReason')=='finish'];usage={t:mean([r['types'][t] for r in finish]) for t in ['call','valueAction','changeFounder','raiseMoney']};values=collections.Counter(v for r in rows for v in r.get('values',[]));founders={}
for r in rows:
 for fid,v in r.get('founderMovement',{}).items():
  a=founders.setdefault(fid,{'founder':fid,'gamesWithMovement':0,'forward':0,'backward':0});a['gamesWithMovement']+=1;a['forward']+=v.get('forward',0);a['backward']+=v.get('backward',0)
metrics={'summary':summary,'completedActionMeans':usage,'cutoffs':dict(collections.Counter(r.get('cutoff') for r in rows if r['status']=='censored')),'valuePlays':dict(values),'founderMovement':list(founders.values())};(p/'metrics.json').write_text(json.dumps(metrics,indent=2));print(json.dumps(metrics['summary'][0]));
if not (p/'sample-review.json').exists():sys.exit()
reviews=json.loads((p/'sample-review.json').read_text());attempts=json.loads((p/'sample-index.json').read_text());manifest=json.loads((p/'manifest.json').read_text());complete=[r for r in attempts if r['status']=='complete'];a=summary[0]
esc=html.escape
def table(rs,keys):return '<table><tr>'+''.join('<th>'+esc(k)+'</th>' for k in keys)+'</tr>'+''.join('<tr>'+''.join('<td>'+esc(str(r[k]) if r.get(k) is not None else '—')+'</td>' for k in keys)+'</tr>' for r in rs)+'</table>'
old=[json.loads(s) for s in (p/'baseline-v137-games.jsonl').read_text().splitlines()];oldmap={(r['seed'],r['players'],r['cohort']):r for r in old};pairs=[(oldmap[(r['seed'],r['players'],r['cohort'])],r) for r in finish if oldmap[(r['seed'],r['players'],r['cohort'])].get('endReason')=='finish'];paired=[{'metric':k,'v137':mean([x[k] for x,y in pairs]),'v138':mean([y[k] for x,y in pairs])} for k in ['range','thirdLag','actions']]
metrics['matchedFinishers']={'games':len(pairs),'results':paired};metrics['discardRollMeanCompleted']=mean([r['discardRolls'] for r in finish]);metrics['stallLegs']=dict(collections.Counter(r['leg'] for r in rows if r['status']=='stalled'));(p/'metrics.json').write_text(json.dumps(metrics,indent=2))
a=summary[0];supplement=json.loads((p/'supplement-index.json').read_text());suppComplete=[r for r in supplement if r['status']=='complete']
body=f'<h1>v138 · Discard a card, activate its company</h1><p>Nine cards/company · five starting cards · three drawn per leg · run-01</p><p><b>{a["finished"]}/60 games reached 24; {a["stalled"]}/60 stalled; {a["failed"]} errors.</b> Completed races were somewhat tighter and shorter, but the change restores an empty-hand bottleneck. It does not yet produce a reliably tight game.</p>'
body+='<h2>The implemented rule</h2><p>Every action spends one deal-flow card. Ordinary funding issues a share in its matching company and grants two chosen dice. For a value, founder change or capital call, resolve that action completely—including any share purchases and their growth—then activate the discarded company with exactly one bland die and no new share. Its before/after founders and explicit reactions work normally, sharing once-per-round limits with purchases. Resolve this activation before checking leg/end conditions. Public slots still refill; private cards are drawn only at leg ends.</p>'
body+='<h2>Is it tighter?</h2>'+table([{'metric':'Reached 24','v137':'28/60','v138':'20/60'},{'metric':'First–last, completed games','v137':'22.32','v138':a['gap']},{'metric':'First–third, completed games','v137':'13.89','v138':a['third']},{'metric':'Median actions, completed games','v137':'60.5','v138':a['actionsMedian']},{'metric':'P90 actions, completed games','v137':'229','v138':a['actionsP90']}],['metric','v137','v138'])
body+='<p>These averages have different survivor populations. v137 had 32 capital-loop research cutoffs, not empty-hand stalls. v138 had 40 true empty-hand stalls, with cards still undealt; none is counted as a tight finish. No unrequested refill or settlement was added.</p>'
body+=f'<p>For the {len(pairs)} matched seed/player/policy combinations that reached 24 in both versions:</p>'+table(paired,['metric','v137','v138'])+'<p>This paired subset also improves, but remains selected and small. The study changes both the rule and the bot’s discard selection, so it cannot isolate a rules-only causal effect. No confidence claim about optimal human play follows.</p>'
body+='<h2>Player count matters</h2>'+table([r for r in summary if r['policy']=='all' and r['players']!='all'],['players','games','finished','stalled','gap','third','actionsMedian','actionsP90'])
body+='<p>Four-player games now finish 15/20 (previously 13/20), with mean first–last 20 and first–third 9.13. Two-player games finish 0/20. Two players have only ten cards before the first gate; their single-die support activations are often insufficient to get three companies to 8. The deck’s nine-per-company supply cannot help until another leg is unlocked.</p><p>The mechanism adds movement, but does not force it into the last-place company. Players select discards to benefit their portfolios. Values can simultaneously push laggards backward or issue extra shares in favorites, and founders amplify those moves. The finishing laggard averages 4 rather than 1.68: better, still well behind 24.</p>'
body+='<details><summary>Action use, prices and policy breakdown</summary><p>Completed-game mean action counts:</p>'+table([usage],list(usage))+f'<p>Mean discarded-card rolls per completed game: {metrics["discardRollMeanCompleted"]}. A discarded-card roll is not a new share or auction. Prices below include sold auctions from all attempted games.</p>'+table([r for r in summary if r['policy']!='all'],['players','policy','games','finished','stalled','gap','third','auctionMean','auctionMedian','auctionP90'])+'</details>'
body+='<details><summary>Founder and value data</summary><p>Raw value plays across all attempts; not exposure-normalized strength:</p>'+table([{'value':k,'plays':v} for k,v in values.most_common()],['value','plays'])+'<p>Founder movement ledger totals, including setup. gamesWithMovement counts ledger presence rather than market exposure. Attribution can overlap; do not sum this as disjoint movement or infer causal card strength.</p>'+table(list(founders.values()),['founder','gamesWithMovement','forward','backward'])+'</details>'
body+=f'<h2>Ten completed games, reviewed</h2><p>The fixed ten sample slots yielded {len(complete)} completed games across {len(attempts)} attempts. A separately frozen supplemental selection yielded {len(suppComplete)} four-player completions in {len(supplement)} attempts. All attempts are retained and replay-verified; supplemental games are excluded from primary metrics. This overrepresents four-player survivors. Reviews also include an unfinished diagnostic.</p><p><a href="supplement-protocol.json">Supplement protocol</a> · <a href="supplement-index.json">Supplement attempts</a></p>'
for r in reviews:
 seed=r['seed'];body+=f'<details><summary>Game {seed}</summary><p>{esc(r["review"])}</p><a href="samples/{seed}.json">Full ordered events and decisions</a> · <a href="samples/{seed}-replay.json">Importable replay</a></details>'
body+='<h2>Interpretation</h2><p>Promising for four players: more completion, shorter games and a tighter leading pack. Not balanced overall: large laggard gaps and complete failure to finish in the two-player cohort. The next discriminating experiment is an explicit way to draw when hands empty, holding the current movement rule fixed; that has not been implemented.</p>'
body+='<details><summary>Protocol, reproducibility and limits</summary><p>60 primary games: seeds 8101–8110 × 2/3/4 players ×balanced self-play/mixed lineups, rotated by seed. Same interactive-quality policy in browser and simulator. The bot evaluates the extra bland activation from current state and combines it with existing action estimates, without a full joint search of action→discard outcomes. Existing generic value/hire estimates remain heuristic.</p><p>Provisional targets: ≥95% reach24; mean first–last≤16 and first–third≤8 among finishers. Completion and spread targets remain unmet. Decisions capped at 2,000; the v137 capital-only cutoff is disabled because capital now advances a company. No rules changed during this cohort.</p><p>Frozen source: '+esc(manifest['source'])+'</p><p><a href="manifest.json">Manifest</a> · <a href="games.jsonl">Primary records</a> · <a href="metrics.json">Metrics</a> · <a href="sample-index.json">All original sample attempts</a> · <a href="runtime.json">Runtime</a> · <a href="source/scripts/mild-dice-study.js">Frozen runner</a></p><pre>node scripts/mild-dice-study.js NEW_DIRECTORY\nnode scripts/discard-supplement.js NEW_DIRECTORY\npython3 scripts/discard-dice-report.py NEW_DIRECTORY</pre><p>Renderer requires authored sample-review.json and the v137 baseline records; a baseline copy is included with this report. Tests cover action-before-roll ordering, forced single bland die, no additional share, founder round limits, atomic rejection, and resolution before terminal settlement.</p></details>'
(p/'report.html').write_text('<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>v138 discard-growth study</title><style>body{font:17px/1.55 system-ui;max-width:1060px;margin:40px auto;padding:0 24px;background:#f8f6ef;color:#243029}h1{line-height:1.2}table{border-collapse:collapse;display:block;overflow:auto;font-size:14px}td,th{padding:8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ccc;text-align:left}details{margin:18px 0;padding:16px;background:white;border:1px solid #ccc;border-radius:8px}summary{font-weight:bold;cursor:pointer}a{color:#17624a}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere}</style>'+body+'</html>')
